        "original_id": "026148e8-c5c6-598c-a9c9-5d278803db7b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: H. P. Lovecraft, Timothy Leary, August Derleth, Donald Wandrei\n- Organizations: Arkham House\n- Places: Sauk City, Wisconsin\n- Topics: horror fiction, psychedelic drugs, weird fiction, publishing\n\nFacts:\n- H. P. Lovecraft was born on August 20, 1890, and he was an American author who achieved posthumous fame through influential works of horror fiction.\n- Timothy Leary was born on October 22, 1920, and he was an American psychologist and writer known for advocating exploration of the therapeutic potential of psychedelic drugs under controlled conditions.\n- Arkham House was founded in 1939 in Sauk City, Wisconsin, by August Derleth and Donald Wandrei.\n- Arkham House is a publishing house specializing in weird fiction.\n- Arkham House was created to preserve the best fiction of H. P. Lovecraft in hardcover.\n- H. P. Lovecraft died on March 15, 1937.\n- Timothy Leary died on May 31, 1996.",
